<nav class="pager"><span></span><a class="next" href="chapter-01.html">1. The new Name type →</a></nav>
<section><h2 id="overview">Overview</h2><h3>Where this change sits</h3>
<p><code>Greeter</code> builds the greeting text from whatever string the caller passes. This change puts a <code>Name</code> type between the caller and <code>Greeter</code>.</p>
<figure class="diagram"><pre class="mermaid" data-source="flowchart LR
  Caller --&gt; Name --&gt; Greeter.greet
  classDef new fill:#dafbe1,stroke:#1a7f37
  classDef changed fill:#fff8c5,stroke:#9a6700
  class Name new
  class Greeter.greet changed">flowchart LR
  Caller --&gt; Name --&gt; Greeter.greet
  classDef new fill:#dafbe1,stroke:#1a7f37
  classDef changed fill:#fff8c5,stroke:#9a6700
  class Name new
  class Greeter.greet changed</pre></figure>
<p>Green is new, yellow is changed; the caller is untouched.</p>
<h3>Why this change</h3>
<p>Passing a raw <code>String</code> let callers send empty or malformed names. Bugs showed up far from the call site.</p>
<h3>What changes</h3>
<p>Introduce a <code>Name</code> record and make <code>Greeter.greet</code> accept only that type. Callers must construct a <code>Name</code>, so validation happens once, at the boundary.</p>
<h3>How to read this report</h3>
<p>Top to bottom: the new type first, then the call site that adopts it, then the class it replaces. Docs and the migration table close the report.</p></section>
<section><h2 id="key-terms">New terms</h2><dl class="glossary"><dt>Name</dt><dd>New value object wrapping a person&#39;s name, so callers cannot pass an arbitrary string.</dd></dl></section>
<section><h2 id="how-to-test">How to test locally</h2><pre><code class="language-bash">mvn -q test</code></pre></section>
<section><h2 id="chapters">Chapters</h2><ol class="chapter-list"><li data-files="src/Name.java"><a href="chapter-01.html">1. The new Name type</a> <span class="muted">1 file, 1 note</span><div class="intro"><p>Everything else depends on this record, so it comes first. It is the type the rest of the change passes around.</p></div></li><li data-files="src/Greeter.java"><a href="chapter-02.html">2. Greeter adopts Name</a> <span class="muted">1 file, 2 notes</span><div class="intro"><p>The only call site. Note the accessor call replacing direct string use; it follows the record because it consumes it.</p></div></li><li data-files="src/Legacy.java"><a href="chapter-03.html">3. Legacy removed</a> <span class="muted">1 file, 1 note</span><div class="intro"><p>Dead class with no references, so removing it is safe. It comes after the call site to show nothing else used it.</p></div></li><li data-files="README.md"><a href="chapter-04.html">4. Usage docs</a> <span class="muted">1 file, 0 notes</span><div class="intro"><p>README gains the build command. Only the usage hunk matters here; the title tweak is in the appendix.</p></div></li><li data-files=""><a href="chapter-05.html">5. Migration checklist</a><div class="intro"><p>Steps for downstream callers, as a table. Read after the code so the actions make sense.</p></div></li><li><a href="other-changes.html">Other changes</a> <span class="muted">6 files</span></li></ol></section>
<nav class="pager"><span></span><a class="next" href="chapter-01.html">1. The new Name type →</a></nav>
</main>
</div>
